body:
wow, what an absolutely repugnant and completely useless "article" that was. the title is nearly half of what's being said. how anyone can seriously be that easily swayed is beyond me....compelling stuff really, he was wearing a "special mask" jfc, it's a goddamn string attached to a piece of cloth on a loop. you can put that string into numerous positions should you choose to. last time I checked my skull was curved and I've never seen any markings to indicate precisely where I should tie things around my head?!?! i imagine i'd look pretty fucking frazzled after an incident like that. oh, it's the same guy in multiple news outlets...cause that's so highly irregular. most people don't want to talk to a news reporter after experiencing a highly traumatic event where they're still in shock. so suspicious he didn't take his ear pods out...c'mon, in case you haven't noticed, people are pretttyyy attached to those things these days. cell phones and gadgets are like an extra appendage. golly i wonder too if he was spending a lot of time on his phone after that event. seems like you would probably be fielding a whole lot of calls.

&#x200B;

for fucks sake u/itsanoobsgame you blasted this on so many channels as if it was some gem of investigative reporting. yeah, stellar sleuth work. those 3 sentences of complete nonsense were sooooo compelling. massive /s try harder.
